                    <chunk name="param_output" index="9">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The vegetation the crowns leave out — hedges, shrubs, young trees from 0.5 m up — one closed mesh per cluster of 2 m columns that stand on the ground and rise to the tallest return, none under a crown, none inside a footprint. Plug into the Tree component's Geometry with a shrub species (Hedge / shrub). Read only from a cloud that classifies vegetation (ASPRS 3-5): where the trees are unclassified points beside buildings, a low one would also be a car or a fence, so none is read. Lawn under 0.5 m is not geometry: it is the surface layers' ground cover. Together with Tree Crowns this is all the vegetation the cloud holds; the Report says what was read.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6aec398f-f76a-41c1-9aba-b18a4550e098</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Low Vegetation</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Low</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
