                    <chunk name="param_output" index="11">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The WHOLE ground as one welded mesh over the whole Domain: no layer is cut out of it and no footprint is either. It is the surface's own triangulation with every triangle at the height of the ground at its corners, so where Terrain or a Layers mesh exists the two agree exactly, a flattened pond is as level here as there, and under a building it is the plane through the ground the walls stand on at the footprint's corners (not the roof). Terrain stays the ground OUTSIDE buildings and layers; this is the ground they all stand on, to look at, to drape something on or to read heights from. Not drawn in this component's preview (it lies under the other parts); kept with the cached surface.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">cea088a0-e206-4513-b7e4-e895dbfb467c</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Full Terrain</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Ground</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
